KERN RUNTIME EXECUTABLE (KRX) SYSCALL EXCEPTION

  As a special exception, the copyright holders of the Kern microkernel
  give you permission to use, copy, modify, and distribute third-party
  KRX application programs that interact with the kernel exclusively
  through the published KRX Application Binary Interface (KRX-ABI)
  system call table ("KrxApiTable"), without those application programs
  being considered derivative works of the kernel under the GPL.

  This exception applies ONLY to standalone third-party KRX userland
  applications (.krx executables) that:

    1. Interact with the kernel solely through the published KRX-ABI
       system call table (KrxApiTable) and its documented primitives;

    2. Do NOT include, embed, copy, or statically link any kernel source
       code, driver source code, or library source code from this
       repository; and

    3. Do NOT modify, extend, or replace any kernel, driver, or platform
       component of the Kern system.

  This exception does NOT apply to, and the full terms of the GPL v3
  remain in force for:

    • The kernel itself and all code under src/kernel/
    • All hardware drivers under src/driver/
    • All platform abstraction layers under src/platform/
    • All libraries under src/lib/
    • The firmware runtime under src/firmware/
    • Any code that includes, links against, or is derived from
      the above components
    • Any modifications or forks of the kernel or its subsystems
    • Any KRX applications that are bundled with, distributed as part
      of, or considered integral to the Kern operating system

  If you create or distribute a modified version of the Kern kernel,
  drivers, platform layers, libraries, or firmware, your modifications
  are subject to the full terms of the GPL v3 and you must release
  the complete corresponding source code.

  If in doubt, it is GPL v3.

